<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Problem Setup: Outcome-Based Bandit</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Arms, outcomes, and partition.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a (large) set of arms with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|=K</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{1,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{1,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a (small) set of <em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">outcomes</em> with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\ll K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\ll K</annotation></semantics></math>.
There is an unknown partition mapping <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathcal{A}\to\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathcal{A}\to\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each outcome <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote its class (preimage) and size by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}:=\phi^{-1}(o),\qquad s_{o}:=|\mathcal{A}_{o}|,\qquad\sum_{o=1}^{m}s_{o}=K." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}:=\phi^{-1}(o),\qquad s_{o}:=|\mathcal{A}_{o}|,\qquad\sum_{o=1}^{m}s_{o}=K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The partitions are mutually exclusive, i.e., for any <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o,o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o,o^{\prime}\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\neq o^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\neq o^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}\cap\mathcal{A}_{o^{\prime}}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}\cap\mathcal{A}_{o^{\prime}}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Define its mass <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o}:=s_{o}/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o}:=s_{o}/K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Partitions may be imbalanced (the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are arbitrary).
We will also consider the balanced special case <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{o}=K/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{o}=K/m</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rewards depend only on the outcome:
pulling arm <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a stochastic reward <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R\mid a]=\mu\big(\phi(a)\big)=:\mu(o)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R\mid a]=\mu\big(\phi(a)\big)=:\mu(o),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and we assume <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R-\mu(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R-\mu(o)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian (for example, Bernoulli).
Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}:=\max_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\mu(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}:=\max_{o\in\mathcal{O}}\mu(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}\in\arg\max_{o}\mu(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}\in\arg\max_{o}\mu(o)</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal outcome.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interaction protocol.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each round <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, a (possibly randomized) policy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> selects an arm <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the history
<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t-1}:=\{(A_{s},O_{s},R_{s})\}_{s=1}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t-1}:=\{(A_{s},O_{s},R_{s})\}_{s=1}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{s}:=\phi(A_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{s}:=\phi(A_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The environment then reveals the outcome label <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{t}=\phi(A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{t}=\phi(A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and draws the reward <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(O_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(O_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The filtration is the natural one generated by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Performance metric (pseudo-regret).</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudo-regret of policy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> over horizon <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{T}(\pi):=T\,\mu^{\star}-\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mu\big(\phi(A_{t})\big)\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\mu^{\star}-\mu\big(O_{t}\big)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{T}(\pi):=T\,\mu^{\star}-\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mu\big(\phi(A_{t})\big)\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\left[\mu^{\star}-\mu\big(O_{t}\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We will also use the discovery time of an outcome <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{o}:=\inf\{t\geq 1:O_{t}=o\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{o}:=\inf\{t\geq 1:O_{t}=o\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with the convention <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf\emptyset=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf\emptyset=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
These stopping times quantify the unavoidable delay before the learner first encounters a given outcome under the no-generalization constraint.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LLM reasoning interpretation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each arm <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a full reasoning trace; the mapping <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is its final answer (outcome), and the reward is the verifiable correctness of that answer.
Although the trace space is large, the outcome space <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is small.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Lower Bound</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first show that, even with the small outcome space, in the worst case any algorithm can not avoid paying a regret that is polynomial in the number of arms <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, without any additional assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lower bound for outcome-based bandit)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and a partition <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{A}_{o}\}_{o=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{A}_{o}\}_{o=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with class sizes <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{o}=|\mathcal{A}_{o}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{o}=|\mathcal{A}_{o}|</annotation></semantics></math> and a unique optimal outcome <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\star}\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\star}\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider Bernoulli rewards with means <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(o_{\star})=\tfrac{1}{2}+\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(o_{\star})=\tfrac{1}{2}+\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(o)=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(o)=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\neq o_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\neq o_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exists a universal constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any (possibly randomized) algorithm <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and any horizon <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists some fixed instance <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[R_{T}(\widetilde{\pi};I^{\star})\right]\ \geq\ c\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{\,T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\,\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[R_{T}(\widetilde{\pi};I^{\star})\right]\ \geq\ c\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{\,T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\,\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Draw an instance by placing the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> optimal arms uniformly at random among the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> arm indices (keeping all other classes fixed).
By <span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:yao-minimax, it suffices to lower-bound the expected regret of an <em id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">arbitrary deterministic</em> policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> under this distribution; the resulting lower bound then holds for some fixed instance <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> against any randomized algorithm <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> be the index of the first pull from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Before time <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> every reward is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>-suboptimal in expectation, hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R_{T}(\pi)]\ \geq\ \Delta\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ =\ \Delta\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R_{T}(\pi)]\ \geq\ \Delta\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ =\ \Delta\sum_{t=1}^{T}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the random placement, the event <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\tau_{\star}&gt;t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{\star}&gt;t\}</annotation></semantics></math> is “no optimal arm among the first <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> draws without replacement,” so</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ =\ \frac{\frac{(K-s_{\star})!}{(K-s_{\star}-t)!}}{\frac{K!}{(K-t)!}}=\prod_{i=0}^{t-1}\frac{K-s_{\star}-i}{K-i}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ =\ \frac{\frac{(K-s_{\star})!}{(K-s_{\star}-t)!}}{\frac{K!}{(K-t)!}}=\prod_{i=0}^{t-1}\frac{K-s_{\star}-i}{K-i}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq K/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq K/2</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{K-s_{\star}-i}{K-i}\ \geq\ \frac{K-s_{\star}-t}{K-t}\ \geq\ 1-\frac{2s_{\star}}{K}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{K-s_{\star}-i}{K-i}\ \geq\ \frac{K-s_{\star}-t}{K-t}\ \geq\ 1-\frac{2s_{\star}}{K}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">hence <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ \big(1-\tfrac{2s_{\star}}{K}\big)^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ \big(1-\tfrac{2s_{\star}}{K}\big)^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}:=\min\big\{\,T,\ \lfloor\tfrac{K}{4s_{\star}}\rfloor\,\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}:=\min\big\{\,T,\ \lfloor\tfrac{K}{4s_{\star}}\rfloor\,\big\}</annotation></semantics></math> (note <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\star}\leq K/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\star}\leq K/2</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\star}\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\star}\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>). Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t^{\star})\ \geq\ \Big(1-\frac{2s_{\star}}{K}\Big)^{K/(4s_{\star})}\ \geq\ e^{-1/2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t^{\star})\ \geq\ \Big(1-\frac{2s_{\star}}{K}\Big)^{K/(4s_{\star})}\ \geq\ e^{-1/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ =\ \sum_{t=1}^{T}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ \sum_{t=1}^{t^{\star}}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ t^{\star}\,\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t^{\star})\ \geq\ c_{0}\,\min\left\{T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ =\ \sum_{t=1}^{T}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ \sum_{t=1}^{t^{\star}}\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t)\ \geq\ t^{\star}\,\Pr(\tau_{\star}&gt;t^{\star})\ \geq\ c_{0}\,\min\left\{T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for a universal constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{0}=e^{-1/2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}=e^{-1/2}/4</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now combining everything,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{I}\left[R_{T}(\pi)\right]\ \geq\ \Delta\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ \geq\ c_{0}\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{I}\left[R_{T}(\pi)\right]\ \geq\ \Delta\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}\right]\ \geq\ c_{0}\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{T,\ \frac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then by <span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:yao-minimax, for any randomized algorithm <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a fixed instance <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in the support of the above distribution such that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[R_{T}(\widetilde{\pi};I^{\star})\right]\ \geq\ c\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{T,\tfrac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[R_{T}(\widetilde{\pi};I^{\star})\right]\ \geq\ c\,\Delta\cdot\min\left\{T,\tfrac{K}{s_{\star}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Balanced Partitions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the previous lower bound comes from the imbalance of the partitions: the polynomial dependence on <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is due to the small (constant) size of the optimal class <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now show that if the partitions are balanced, i.e., <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{o}=K/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{o}=K/m</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can design an algorithm whose regret is independent of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{assumption}</span>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[Balanced partition]
Assume <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}_{o}|=s=K/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}_{o}|=s=K/m</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Rewards depend only on the outcome
and when an arm <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is pulled we observe its outcome <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\phi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\phi(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and the reward.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Balanced Outcome UCB</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize:
<math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (set of discovered outcomes, initially <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>);
<math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]</annotation></semantics></math> (representative arm for outcome <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, initially undefined);
<math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for each discovered <math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> (both <math id="alg1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> initially);
<math id="alg1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (set of unseen arms, initially <math id="alg1.l1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Discovery phase
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               Pick <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(U)</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\leftarrow U\setminus\{A_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\leftarrow U\setminus\{A_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               Pull <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; observe outcome <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\phi(A_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\phi(A_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and reward <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\notin\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\notin\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
   
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else<span id="alg1.l9.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Outcome-level UCB
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               For each <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               Pull <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>; observe <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;  <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o_{t}}\leftarrow n_{o_{t}}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o_{t}}\leftarrow n_{o_{t}}+1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg1.l12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}}{n_{o_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}}{n_{o_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Upper bound under <span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>ass:balanced)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming <span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>ass:balanced, <span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:balanced-ucb satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O(\sqrt{mT\log T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O(\sqrt{mT\log T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We decompose regret into a <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">discovery</em> part (before all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes have been observed)
and a <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">bandit</em> part (afterwards, when we run UCB on the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> outcome representatives).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first round at which the set of observed outcomes equals <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>
(i.e., the time to discover all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes).
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal outcome with mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{o}:=\mu^{\star}-\mu(o)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{o}:=\mu^{\star}-\mu(o)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">While <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> the algorithm draws <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">unseen</em> arms uniformly without replacement.
Because the partition is balanced, the revealed outcome sequence is distributed as a uniformly
random permutation of a multiset that contains exactly <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/m</annotation></semantics></math> copies of each label.
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{cc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>cc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{cc}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the coupon-collector time to see all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> labels <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">under i.i.d. sampling
with replacement</em> where each label has probability <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math> per draw.
We will show (<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p3.1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:cc-coupling) that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq\mathbb{E}[T_{\mathrm{cc}}]\leq m(\log m+1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>cc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq\mathbb{E}[T_{\mathrm{cc}}]\leq m(\log m+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since per-round pseudo-regret is at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (rewards lie in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>), the discovery contribution satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq m(\log m+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq m(\log m+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then at time <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> the algorithm has stored one <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">representative</em> arm per outcome.
From that time onward it never samples unseen arms; it only chooses among the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> representatives.
Because rewards depend only on outcome, this reduces <em id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">exactly</em> to an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-armed stochastic bandit.
Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}:=\max\{0,\,T-\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}:=\max\{0,\,T-\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of post-discovery rounds (random, but <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>).
The algorithm runs UCB on the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> arms with index
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> as specified in <span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:balanced-ucb.
We will bound the regret in these <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds by a standard UCB bound (<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p5.1.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:ucb-gapfree):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\ \Big|\ \tau_{\mathrm{disc}}\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T^{\prime}\,\log T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\ \Big|\ \tau_{\mathrm{disc}}\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T^{\prime}\,\log T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Taking expectations and using <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">And we conclude the proof by summing <span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>eq:disc-regret and <span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8.1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>eq:postdisc-regret-exp, but noting that <span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p8.1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>eq:postdisc-regret-exp is the dominant term.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Inbalanced Partition under Strong Generalization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our previous results are all established under a non-generalization scenario, where the update of arms in the same outcome partition is independent. This is not realistic under the LLM reasoning setting, since the update of one reasoning path (arm) can affect the other paths that lead to the same answer (outcome). We now show that this generalization capability is the key to demonstrating the benefit of outcome-based exploration, where previously under the worst case scenario the regret must depend on <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. We start with a strong generalization assumption, where we assume that once an outcome is observed, the entire class of arms leading to that outcome is identified.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{assumption}</span>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[Strong generalization]
When the learner pulls an arm <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and observes the outcome
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\phi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\phi(a)</annotation></semantics></math>, it henceforth knows the entire preimage <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}=\phi^{-1}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}=\phi^{-1}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and can (i) <em id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">route</em> to <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>
by selecting any arm in <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (ii) <em id="A1.SS4.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exclude</em> <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> from future fresh probes. For any outcome
<math id="A1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> not yet observed, the learner cannot route to <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> nor exclude it a priori.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, with strong generalization, once an outcome is observed, the whole outcome partition is discovered, and then it can be treated as a single arm in the future. Then the problem reduces to an <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-armed bandit problem. We provide the algorithm in <span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:pa-ucb, which enjoys the following regret guarantee.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Partition-Aware UCB under Strong Generalization</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize:
<math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (set of discovered outcomes, initially <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>);
<math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]</annotation></semantics></math> (representative arm for <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, undefined until discovery);
<math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\in\mathbb{N},\ \hat{\mu}_{o}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\in\mathbb{N},\ \hat{\mu}_{o}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (both <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> initially);
<math id="alg2.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (pool of arms eligible for fresh probes, initially <math id="alg2.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg2.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Discovery phase
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               Pick any <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}\in U</annotation></semantics></math>; pull <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; observe <math id="alg2.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o=\phi(A_{t}),r_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o=\phi(A_{t}),r_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\notin\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\notin\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\leftarrow U\setminus\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\leftarrow U\setminus\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>
   
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else<span id="alg2.l11.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Outcome-level UCB
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               For each <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="alg2.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               Pull <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>; observe <math id="alg2.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; update <math id="alg2.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o_{t}},\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o_{t}},\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Regret upper bound under strong generalization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming <span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>ass:strong-gen, Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.4 Inbalanced Partition under Strong Generalization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Results ‣ Outcome-based Exploration for LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the (random) time the set of discovered outcomes first equals <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction, as soon as a new outcome <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> is observed, the algorithm removes the entire class <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> from
the fresh-probe pool <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence each subsequent fresh probe must land in an outcome not yet discovered.
Therefore <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}\leq m</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely: at most one fresh probe per outcome is needed.
Per-round pseudo-regret is at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the discovery contribution is bounded deterministically by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\leq\min\{T,\,m\}\leq m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\leq\min\{T,\,m\}\leq m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">At time <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> the algorithm has one representative per outcome.
From then on it only selects among these <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> representatives using the UCB index
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This reduces exactly to an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-armed
stochastic bandit. By <span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:ucb-gapfree, the post-discovery outcome-UCB satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq O\left(\sqrt{m\,T\,\log T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Again by noting that the post-discovery contribution is the dominant term, we complete the proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Soft Generalization: Algorithm and Upper Bound</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The above example of strong generalization is idealized as it is unreasonable to believe that one witness of the outcome is sufficient for generalization towards all related arms. We now consider a more realistic <em id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">soft generalization</em> model. Intuitively, soft generalization states that instead of being able to exclude the entire class <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> upon first observing outcome <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, the learner can only exclude a fraction of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{assumption}</span>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[Soft generalization]
Upon first observing an outcome <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, the learner can (i) route perfectly to <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> by re-pulling the observed arm; and (ii) exclude only a fraction of <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{o}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{o}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> of the arms in <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> from future fresh probes.

When <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{o}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{o}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, this reduces to strong generalization (<span id="A1.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>ass:strong-gen); when <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{o}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{o}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>, this reduces to no generalization. Note that this assumption is rather unconventional: it is an assumption on the learner instead of the environment. However, this is a more suitable assumption here because it is indeed trying to model the generalization capability of the learner (LLM). With this we provide the soft-exclusion outcome-UCB algorithm in <span id="A1.SS5.p2.2.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:se-oucb and analyze its performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Soft-Exclusion Outcome-UCB</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize: <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (discovered outcomes; initially <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>);
<math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]</annotation></semantics></math> (representative of <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>; undefined until discovery);
<math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n_{o},\hat{\mu}_{o})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n_{o},\hat{\mu}_{o})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg3.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (both <math id="alg3.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> initially);
<math id="alg3.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (pool available for fresh probes; initially <math id="alg3.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{R}|&lt;m</annotation></semantics></math> and we are in <em id="alg3.l3.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">discovery mode</em> <span id="alg3.l3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
               Draw <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly from <math id="alg3.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, pull it, observe <math id="alg3.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o=\phi(A_{t}),r_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o=\phi(A_{t}),r_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\notin\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\notin\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\{o\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg3.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o]\leftarrow A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg3.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg3.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
                 (Soft exclusion) remove any <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{o}\subseteq\mathcal{A}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{o}\subseteq\mathcal{A}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg3.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E_{o}|=\rho_{o}s_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E_{o}|=\rho_{o}s_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\leftarrow U\setminus E_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\leftarrow U\setminus E_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o}\leftarrow n_{o}+1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg3.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}\leftarrow\hat{\mu}_{o}+\dfrac{r_{t}-\hat{\mu}_{o}}{n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math>
   
</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               For each <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="alg3.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o):=\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o):=\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{\dfrac{2\log t}{\max\{1,n_{o}\}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>UCB</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}\in\arg\max_{o\in\mathcal{R}}\ \mathrm{UCB}_{t}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               pull <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rep</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rep}[o_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>; observe <math id="alg3.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; update <math id="alg3.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{o_{t}},\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{o_{t}},\hat{\mu}_{o_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Upper bound under soft generalization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming soft generalization (Assumption <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5 Soft Generalization: Algorithm and Upper Bound ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Results ‣ Outcome-based Exploration for LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>), <span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:se-oucb satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}+\sqrt{mT\log T}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}+\sqrt{mT\log T}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\rho}:=\sum_{o\neq o_{\star}}\rho_{o}p_{o}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\rho}:=\sum_{o\neq o_{\star}}\rho_{o}p_{o}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To prove this theorem, we first prove the stopping time that we discover the optimal outcome:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First hit of the optimal outcome)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With <span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>alg:se-oucb, let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> be the index (number of fresh probes) of the
first pull that lands in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the pool of arms available for fresh probes just <em id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">before</em> the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th fresh probe, and let
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> be the (random) union of all excluded sets <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> over non-optimal outcomes <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\neq o_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\neq o_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that have been
discovered prior to time <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition of soft exclusion, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E|\leq\sum_{o\neq o_{\star}}\rho_{o}s_{o}=K\bar{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E|\leq\sum_{o\neq o_{\star}}\rho_{o}s_{o}=K\bar{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any history up to time <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}&gt;t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}&gt;t-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then no arm from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> has been drawn yet, so
all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{o_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{o_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> optimal arms remain in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The next fresh probe samples uniformly from <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\text{hit }\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}\text{ at probe }t\mid\tau_{\star}&gt;t-1,\ \mathcal{H}_{t-1})=\frac{s_{o_{\star}}}{|U_{t}|}\geq\frac{s_{o_{\star}}}{K-|E|}\geq\frac{p_{o_{\star}}}{1-\bar{\rho}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">hit </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> at probe </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\text{hit }\mathcal{A}_{o_{\star}}\text{ at probe }t\mid\tau_{\star}&gt;t-1,\ \mathcal{H}_{t-1})=\frac{s_{o_{\star}}}{|U_{t}|}\geq\frac{s_{o_{\star}}}{K-|E|}\geq\frac{p_{o_{\star}}}{1-\bar{\rho}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The first inequality uses <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{t}|\leq K-|E|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{t}|\leq K-|E|</annotation></semantics></math> (we can only remove arms, via exclusions and previous draws),
and the second uses <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E|\leq K\bar{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E|\leq K\bar{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the conditional success probability at each probe is
<em id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">uniformly</em> lower bounded by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o_{\star}}/(1-\bar{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o_{\star}}/(1-\bar{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math>, regardless of the discovery order of non-optimal outcomes.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a geometric random variable with parameter <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{o_{\star}}/(1-\bar{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{o_{\star}}/(1-\bar{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> (counting the number of trials until
the first success). By the usual domination argument for inhomogeneous Bernoulli sequences with per-trial success
probability bounded below,<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                <span id="footnote2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">Formally, if </span><math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> are conditionally independent given the past with
</span><math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(X_{t}=1\mid\mathcal{H}_{t-1})\geq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(X_{t}=1\mid\mathcal{H}_{t-1})\geq\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> for all </span><math id="footnote2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">, then </span><math id="footnote2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{u=1}^{t}(1-X_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{u=1}^{t}(1-X_{u})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> is stochastically dominated by a sum of
i.i.d. </span><math id="footnote2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Bernoulli}(1-\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Bernoulli}(1-\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">, and the first success time is dominated by </span><math id="footnote2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Geom}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Geom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Geom}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span></span></span>
we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\star}\preceq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\star}\preceq G</annotation></semantics></math> (stochastic domination). Taking expectations gives
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq(1-\bar{\rho})/p_{o_{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq(1-\bar{\rho})/p_{o_{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proof of <span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>thm:soft-upper)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decompose the pseudo-regret as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{T}=\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))+\sum_{t=\tau_{\star}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{T}=\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))+\sum_{t=\tau_{\star}}^{T}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the first term, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>o</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{t=1}^{\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}}(\mu^{\star}-\mu(O_{t}))\Big]\leq\mathbb{E}[\min\{T,\tau_{\star}-1\}]\leq\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\star}]\leq\frac{1-\bar{\rho}}{p_{o_{\star}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma A.8 (First hit of the optimal outcome). ‣ A.5 Soft Generalization: Algorithm and Upper Bound ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Results ‣ Outcome-based Exploration for LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>. For the second term, apply <span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\pref</span>lem:ucb-gapfree.
Summing the bounds gives the claim.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all algorithms in this section, we separate the exploration phase (discovering outcomes) and the exploitation phase (outcome-level UCB). This is mainly for ease of presentation and analysis. In practice, the exploration phase can happen naturally with the outcome-level UCB, as the algorithm will always seek unpicked outcomes due to the design of the UCB term.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Technical Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\det}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>det</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\det}</annotation></semantics></math> be a (possibly infinite) set of deterministic algorithms (policies), let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of instances,
and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:\Pi_{\det}\times\mathcal{I}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>det</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:\Pi_{\det}\times\mathcal{I}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be any (measurable) loss functional.
Write <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Pi_{\det})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>det</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Pi_{\det})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\mathcal{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\mathcal{I})</annotation></semantics></math> for distributions over algorithms and instances, respectively.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\widetilde{\pi}\in\Delta(\Pi_{\det})}\ \sup_{I\in\mathcal{I}}\ \mathbb{E}\big[\,L(\widetilde{\pi},I)\,\big]\ \ \geq\ \ \sup_{\mathcal{D}\in\Delta(\mathcal{I})}\ \inf_{\pi\in\Pi_{\det}}\ \mathbb{E}_{I\sim\mathcal{D}}\big[\,L(\pi,I)\,\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>det</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.667em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>≥</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>det</mo></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\widetilde{\pi}\in\Delta(\Pi_{\det})}\ \sup_{I\in\mathcal{I}}\ \mathbb{E}\big[\,L(\widetilde{\pi},I)\,\big]\ \ \geq\ \ \sup_{\mathcal{D}\in\Delta(\mathcal{I})}\ \inf_{\pi\in\Pi_{\det}}\ \mathbb{E}_{I\sim\mathcal{D}}\big[\,L(\pi,I)\,\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.13</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Coupon-collector coupling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Motwani and Raghavan, 1996</a>)</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the balanced partition setting, let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the discovery time when drawing unseen arms
uniformly without replacement. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{cc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>cc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{cc}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the time to observe all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> labels under i.i.d.
sampling with replacement with uniform label distribution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq\mathbb{E}[T_{\mathrm{cc}}]=mH_{m}\leq m(\log m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>disc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>cc</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tau_{\mathrm{disc}}]\leq\mathbb{E}[T_{\mathrm{cc}}]=mH_{m}\leq m(\log m+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.14</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Auer et al. (2002)</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-armed stochastic bandit with rewards in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> that are <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian and means <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mu(o)\}_{o=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mu(o)\}_{o=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Run UCB with index <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{o}+\sqrt{(2\log t)/n_{o}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots,T</annotation></semantics></math> (initializing each arm once).
Then the pseudo-regret satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\sqrt{mT\log T}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R_{T}]\leq O\left(\sqrt{mT\log T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experiment on Hard Dataset</h2>

<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.06941v1/x12.svg" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/122;" width="286" height="122"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Training performance comparison between <math id="A2.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚄𝙲𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙲𝚘𝚗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Batch}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱𝚊𝚝𝚌𝚑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Batch}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A2.F7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{GRPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙶𝚁𝙿𝙾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{GRPO}</annotation></semantics></math> baseline, with <math id="A2.F7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙻𝚕𝚊𝚖𝚊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace">3.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟾</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙸𝚗𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚞𝚌𝚝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}</annotation></semantics></math> on the hard dataset. Left: fraction of questions solved so far; Right: number of different answers sampled so far. The x-axis denotes the number of gradient updates as we train all models fully on-policy. We repeat each experiment with 3 different random seeds and plot the mean performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we compare the training performance between <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚄𝙲𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙲𝚘𝚗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Batch}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱𝚊𝚝𝚌𝚑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Batch}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{GRPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙶𝚁𝙿𝙾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{GRPO}</annotation></semantics></math> baseline on the hard dataset. For <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙻𝚕𝚊𝚖𝚊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace">3.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟾</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙸𝚗𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚞𝚌𝚝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dataset comprises 996 questions in total. We observe the improvement of outcome-based exploration algorithm is even larger than the base model in this hard dataset, in both the number of questions solved and the number of unique solutions explored. However, we remark that this is more of a synthetic setting because training on this hard dataset does not bring meaningful improvement on the test dataset, for all of the baselines. Nevertheless, combining with the results from the medium dataset, our results indicate that exploration is more beneficial in the medium to hard training regime.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Omitted Plots</h2>

<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.06941v1/x13.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/100;" width="234" height="100"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.06941v1/x14.svg" id="A3.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/100;" width="234" height="100"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Training performance comparison between different <math id="A3.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{UCB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚄𝙲𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{UCB}</annotation></semantics></math> variants and the <math id="A3.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{GRPO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙶𝚁𝙿𝙾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{GRPO}</annotation></semantics></math> baseline, with <math id="A3.F8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙻𝚕𝚊𝚖𝚊</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace">3.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟾</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙸𝚗𝚜𝚝𝚛𝚞𝚌𝚝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Llama\text{-}3.1\text{-}8B\text{-}Instruct}</annotation></semantics></math> on the medium dataset (left) and <math id="A3.F8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{Qwen\text{-}2.5\text{-}7B\text{-}Base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚀𝚠𝚎𝚗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace">2.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟽</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙱𝚊𝚜𝚎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{Qwen\text{-}2.5\text{-}7B\text{-}Base}</annotation></semantics></math> on the easy dataset (right). For each subplot: Left: fraction of questions solved so far; Right: number of different answers sampled on the questions that the model has yet to solve (i.e., sample one correct answer historically). The x-axis denotes the number of gradient updates as we train all models fully on-policy. We repeat each experiment with 3 different random seeds and plot the mean performance.</figcaption>
</figure>
