<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Quantitative Results</h2>

<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Quantitative comparison of different baselines on pass@1 and pass@32 at the best checkpoint over three random seeds. We report mean and standard deviation in parentheses. The best mean results are in bold. Note that <math id="A4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚄𝙲𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝙲𝚘𝚗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{UCB\text{-}Con}</annotation></semantics></math> in general achieves the best peak performance.</figcaption>
